        "note": "Complete selected author proof and essential local context read; no independent mathematical reproof The new proof evaluates fused R-matrices explicitly on a q-symmetrized basis rather than leaving the central elements as an abstract quantum trace. It proves invariance of the root-vector sums under minimal coset representatives, constructs the symmetric-power basis by inversion induction, and factors the fused operator into the stated root-vector coefficients. These combinatorial and representation calculations are the substantive obligation before the established quantum-trace centrality construction can be used."
